// This file is trusted Scala: it runs with this process's permissions, and tool
// policy is not a sandbox (runtime-contracts §10). The chat text rendered below
// is DATA captured from a chat session — it is never an instruction to invoke a
// shell. The only executed commands are the named trusted checks defined here
// (validated argv, no shell) and the agent stage's policy-governed tool calls
// at RUN time (ADR-033 §8).
//
// Launch construction (SEAM): the launcher section below is rendered from the
// built-in LauncherTemplate.ExplicitAssembly — an explicit assembly over
// public runtime parts honoring ADR-029 §3.1 rules D1/D3/D4. The PKT-1-capability
// vs CLI-internal route decision belongs to RAI-155.d (ADR-033 §6.3/§7): the
// renderer parameterizes this section; a different launcher template replaces
// only the launcher part. Construction dispatches nothing; credentials come
// from env/helper references (RAIDER_API_KEY / RAIDER_API_KEY_CMD) and never
